    "notes": [
      "Bridge-tied outputs: each speaker between +OUT and -OUT, never to ground; no output filter needed with short speaker leads (ferrite beads on the outputs against EMI).",
      "Gain fixed at 24 dB (internal 18 kΩ input resistance): the input capacitor and 18 kΩ set the low corner, 0.47 µF gives about 19 Hz; a series resistor at the input lowers the gain.",
      "MUTE and SHDN have internal pull-ups: leave them open or drive them low from GPIO.",
      "Wide, short PVDD and PGND traces; never above 5.5 V (four fresh alkaline cells exceed 6 V)."
    ],
    "page": "Typical applications circuit (p. 1); application information (p. 7-9): maximum gain, mute, shutdown, power supply decoupling, input capacitor, VREF bypass capacitor, EMI"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Diodes marks the part not recommended for new designs (PAM8406 is the successor); it stays the amplifier of the ubiquitous PAM8403 boards.",
    "Output pin names with the sign last (datasheet +OUT_L = OUTL+, -OUT_L = OUTL-, likewise right)."
  ],
